{title: 642 - We Praise Thee With Our Minds}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #642 • CLONMEL • 8.5.8.6.8.6.9.6}
{lyricist: Hugh T. McElrath}
{composer: Irish Melody}
{key: Eb}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 642}
{meta: tune CLONMEL}
{meta: meter 8.5.8.6.8.6.9.6}
{meta: category Christian Life - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[Bb]We [Eb]praise Thee [Ddim]with [Bb7]our minds, O Lord,
[Ab]Kept [Gm]sharp [Fm]think Thy [Ddim]thought;
[Ddim]Come, [Eb]Holy [Ddim]Ghost [Bb7]with grace [Eb]outpoured,
[Ab]To [Gm]teach [Fm]what [Eb]Christ [Gm]hath taught.
[Bb]In [Cm]all [Ab]our learning [Bb7]may we [Gm]seek
[Bb]That [Ab]wisdom [Fm]from [Eb]above
[Ddim]Which [Eb]comes [Cm]to all: [Bb]the brave, the meek,
[Ab/Eb]Who [Gm]ask [Eb]in [Fm]faith [Bb7]and love.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Bb]We [Eb]praise Thee [Ddim]thro' [Bb7]our bodies, Lord,
[Ab]Kept [Gm]strong [Eb]to [Fm]do [Ddim]Thy will;
[Ddim]Thy [Eb]Spirit's [Ddim]temples, [Bb7]which [Eb]afford
[Ab]A [Gm]means [Fm]to [Eb]praise [Gm]Thee still.
[Bb]We give [Cm]ourselves, a [Bb7]sacrifice,
[Bb]To [Ab]live [Gm/D]as [Fm]unto [Cm]Thee;
[Ddim]For [Eb]Thou [Cm]alone [Bb]hast paid the price
[Ab/Eb]To [Gm]bring [Eb]salvation [Bb7]free.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[Bb]We [Eb]praise Thee [Ddim]in [Bb7]our hearts, O king,
[Ab]Kept [Gm]pure [Eb]to [Fm]know [Ddim]Thy ways;
[Ddim]And [Eb]raise to [Ddim]Thee [Bb7]a hymn [Eb]to sing
[Ab]Eternally [Gm]Thy praise.
[Bb]Altho [Ab]adoring [Bb7]hearts will [Gm]bow
[Bb]As [Ab]age [Gm/D]on [Fm]ages [Cm]roll;
[Ddim]We [Eb]praise [Cm]Thee in [Bb]our beings now,
[Ab/Eb]Mind, [Gm]body, [Fm]heart, [Bb7]and soul.
{end_of_verse}
